Client Side
The client side of the application is built using React.
Setup:
Navigate to the client directory:      "cd client"
Install the dependencies:     "npm install"
Start the development server:    "npm start"
Available Scripts:
In the client directory, you can run:
- npm start: Runs the app in development mode.
- npm test: Launches the test runner in interactive watch mode.
- npm run build: Builds the app for production to the build folder.
- npm run eject: Ejects the create-react-app configuration.
Server Side:
The server side of the application is built using Node.js and Express.
Setup:
-Navigate to the server directory:  "cd server"
-Install the dependencies:  "npm install"
-Start the server: "node index.js"
API Endpoints
- GET /auctions: Retrieve all auctions.
- POST /auction: Create a new auction.
- POST /bid: Place a bid on an auction.
- GET /auction/:id: Retrieve a specific auction by ID.

Database Schema
The database schema is defined in Schema.js. This file includes the definitions for the various entities involved in the auction process, such as Users, Auctions, and Bids.

